// Three later segments reported, no reordering seen: the reordering window is zero (RFC 8985 6.2: RACK is as quick as
// three duplicates were), so the hole is lost as soon as RACK's round trip has passed since it left, and it has. The
// handshake's ACK 10 ms after the SYN-ACK gives a round trip of 10 ms; the four segments share the stamp 10 ms. The ACK
// at 20 ms reports the last three: RACK's segment is the fourth, its round trip 10 ms, and the first is due at
// 10 + 10 + 0 = 20 ms, now. It is resent on that ACK, with no timer: of 400 outstanding 300 are reported and 100 lost,
// so nothing is in flight; the target is max(400 / 2, 2 * 1448) = 2896, RecoverFS 400 - 300 + 300 = 400, and PRR's
// conservative bound allows the 300 the ACK delivered. Linux marks it on the same ACK: its tcp_rack_reo_wnd is zero
// once sacked_out reaches tp->reordering, three.
0 socket(..., SOCK_STREAM, IPPROTO_TCP) = 3
+0 bind(3, ..., ...) = 0
+0 listen(3, 1) = 0

+0 < S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val 100 ecr 0,nop,wscale 7>
+0 > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,sackOK,TS val 0 ecr 100,nop,wscale 3>
+0.010 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 512 <nop,nop,TS val 110 ecr 0>
+0 accept(3, ..., ...) = 4

+0 write(4, ..., 100) = 100
